> I am a Level 3 Wiz, found a wand of wishing on Level 6.  I have a +2
> quarterstaff, Elven-Mithril Coat, Gauntlets of Power, Boots of Speed
> (armor shop purchases),....my AC is -1.  My Int is 17.  I've read lots
> of the threads about wishing, but hoped to get some specific
> help...that's what everybody's here for right?  It'd really be
> appreciated.

You just got SDSM +2, so you have MR, Reflection, speed, and a pretty
decent AC.  With GoP, you're doing a reasonable amount of damage
with your quarterstaff.  A wish for an artifact weapon is probably not
that
useful right now, considering your first sacrifice gift (Magicbane) is
all you
need.

Here are my suggestions:
blessed fixed +2 Helm of Brilliance
- You only have an intelligence of 17, so increasing this to 18 will
get you
hungerless spellcasting.  It will also help with PW regeneration,
which
will be an issue for you until you ge the quest artifact.

Blessed Magic Marker
- You already have at two-three pieces of armor that you'll want to
keep
all the way to the end of the game. Write "enchant armor" scolls and
enchant the DSM, CoMR, Boots, HoB (if you get it) to +4/+5.  This is
another 10 points of AC easy.  As a wizard, you also have a good
chance of writing the spellbooks mentioned further down, but I
wouldn't
worry about that now.

Amulet of Life Saving
- This is not something I generally wish for, but as a new player
there
are thing out there that you won't expect, and this can save you.
Once.

2 tins of green dragon
- Do you have poison resistance yet?  I know it seems silly to wish
for something like this (and given that you have GoP, you should
simply
eat all recently dead corpses until you get it), but given that you
have
MR and reflection, being fatally poisoned is the only thing I'd
really
worry about.  Eating a tin of green dragon meat solves this issue.


blessed spellbook of Identify
- This one is great for new players, as identifying things is a big
part of
the game.  The only concern is that I tend to go overboard trying to
identify things, and until you get the quest artifact, it's a big mana
drain -
leaving you with no PW to defend yourself.  Note:  You should build a
stock of 10-15 daggers and start practicing throwing them at
everything.
Save the PW for when you need it.

blessed spellbook of charm monster
Turn all the nasties you meet into pets.  'nough said.

Quest artifact:
Either the Eyes of the Overworld or Master Key of Thievery
(depending on your alignment). Both confer useful properties,
but beware of being shocked when picking the up/using them.

Happy Hacking.
